  <aside class="ad-rail" aria-label="Advertisement"><div class="ad-slot ad-slot-rail"></div></aside>
  <div class="wrap article">
    <p class="note"><a href="/guides.html">Guides</a> / Data formats</p>
    <h1>Spreadsheet Files vs Data Files: Which to Use?</h1>
    <p class="lead">Spreadsheets and computer programs often save data in different kinds of file. CSV is a simple table saved as plain text. JSON is a more flexible format that programs use. This guide helps you choose the right one.</p>
    <div class="ad-slot" aria-label="Advertisement"></div>
<h2>CSV: a simple table</h2>
<p>A CSV file is a table saved as plain text. Each line is a row, and commas separate the columns. Spreadsheets can open and save CSV files, which makes them easy to share.</p>
<h2>JSON: data with labels</h2>
<p>A JSON file stores each item with a label, such as name or city. It can also hold lists inside lists. Websites and apps often use JSON to send information to each other.</p>
<h2>Which should you choose?</h2>
<ul>
<li>Use CSV for a simple list or table that you want to open in a spreadsheet.</li>
<li>Use JSON when a program needs to read the file, or the data has groups inside groups.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Common problems when changing one into the other</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Commas inside a name:</strong> a name such as Ravi, Jr. must be wrapped in quotation marks in a CSV file, or it will be split in two.</li>
<li><strong>Numbers:</strong> CSV does not say whether a value is a number or text, so 27 may come out as text.</li>
</ul>
      <section class="worked">
        <h2>Worked example</h2>
        <p>A row in a spreadsheet holds a name 'Ravi, Jr.', a city 'Colombo' and an age of 27. Saved as CSV, the name must be in quotation marks so the comma inside it is not read as a column break. Converted to JSON, each value gets a label, and the age is kept as text.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="faq-list">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <details><summary>Can I open a data file in Excel?</summary><p>Yes. For a simple table, you can open a CSV file directly. Other data files may need to be imported first.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Why did my numbers turn into text?</summary><p>A CSV file does not say what kind of value each cell holds. Your program decides. Check the cells you need as numbers.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which one should a beginner use?</summary><p>For a list you want to open in a spreadsheet, use CSV. Only use JSON when a program asks for it.</p></details>
      </section>
